    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Fried Chicken Day",
    "caption": "Among the many fried chickens in Korea, Yangnyeom, which translates to “seasoned chicken”, is one of the most popular ones. What sets it apart is that this fried chicken is drenched in a fiery red sauce made with aromatics and red pepper paste.\n\nMake Yangnyeom Korean Fried Chicken at home using Magnolia Spicy Fried Chicken. The chicken already comes with a bit of heat, adding a lot of kick and flavor. Coated with peanuts and garnished with spring onions, find all the ingredients you need at #TheMarketplace! \n\nServing Time: 50 minutes\nYield: 3-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 pack Magnolia Spicy Fried Chicken \n½ cup potato starch\n½ tsp. baking powder  \nOil for deep-frying \n1 tsp. garlic, grated \n½ tsp. ginger, grated \n2 tbsps. tomato ketchup\n2 tbsps. gochujang \n1 tbsp. rice syrup \n2 tsps. rice vinegar \n2 tsps. sesame oil \n¼ cup peanuts, chopped \n2 tbsps. spring onions, chopped\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Transfer the flour coating mix that comes with Magnolia Spicy Fried Chicken into a bowl. Combine with potato starch and baking powder. Coat chicken pieces with this. \n2. Preheat oil to 165°C for deep-frying in a large pot.\n3. Meanwhile, combine garlic, ginger, ketchup, gochujang, vinegar and sesame oil. Set aside for coating fried chicken pieces later on. \n4. Once oil is hot, deep-fry coated chicken pieces for 8-10 minutes, or until golden brown and cooked through. Let cool completely. Preheat oil to 185°C. \n5. Double-fry chicken for 2-3 minutes. \n6. Toss to coat with the sauce and peanuts. \n7. Garnish with spring onions. \n\nNo need to fall in line! Order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
