    "layoutCode": "IC2",
    "layoutName": "Hainanese Fried Chicken",
    "category": "RECIPE",
    "categorySource": "inferred",
    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Fried Chicken Day",
    "caption": "One of the reasons why tourists flock to Singapore is because of its hawker center food, and one of the most iconic ones being Hainanese Chicken.\n\nBursting with flavors of ginger, sesame oil, and lemongrass, this recipe for Hainanese Fried Chicken uses Bounty Fresh Everyday Chicken, aromatics, and a whole lot of love. It may take almost an hour and a half to prepare, but the result is super worth it, we promise! Shop the freshest poultry and ingredients at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour and 20 minutes\nYield: 3-4 servings\n\nIngredients\n¼ cup sesame oil\n2 tbsps. salt \n1 tbsp. ginger, grated \n2 tbsps. lemongrass, ends finely chopped \n1 Bounty Fresh Everyday Chicken, deboned \n1 egg \n1½ cups flour \n1 tsp. baking powder \nOil for deep-frying \n\nProcedure\n\n1. Whisk together sesame oil, salt, ginger and lemongrass. Coat Bounty Everyday Chicken with this mixture, and marinate for at least 30 minutes in the chiller. \n2. Whisk together egg and ¼ cup cold water. \n3. Remove marinated Bounty Everyday Chicken from the chiller, and let excess marinade drip off. Dredge with flour, then dip into the egg and water mixture, then into the flour again. Make sure to press the flour coating into the entire chicken. \n4. Preheat oil to 165°C in a large pot or wok. Meanwhile, let the breading of the chicken set. Once oil reaches the prescribed temperature, deep-fry for 10-12 minutes. Drain and let cool.\n5. Bring up the oil temperature to 185°C. Once hot enough, deep-fry again for 2-3 minutes.\n6. Serve as is, or with Hainanese rice and sauces. \n\nNo need to fall in line! Order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
