    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Fried Chicken Day",
    "caption": "Japanese karaage is typically made with skin-on boneless chicken thighs, but in this recipe for Chicken Karaage, we swapped the thighs for cubed chicken breast, seasoned them, coated them with a thin batter, and fried them in UFC Golden Fiesta Palm Oil.\n\nIt’s best to cook these fresh, around an hour and a half before meal-time, to get that exquisite crunch and juicy meat. Find UFC Golden Fiesta Palm Oil, and other types of oil, at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour and 30 minutes\nYield: 3-4 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n300g chicken breast, cubed\n3 tbsps. soy sauce\n2 tbsp. mirin\n1 tbsp. sugar\n1 tbsp. ginger, grated\n2 cloves garlic, grated\n2 cups UFC Golden Fiesta Palm Oil\n1 egg, beaten\n½ cup potato starch\n½ tsp. togarashi\n½ cup mayonnaise\n2 tbsps. milk\n3 tbsps. parsley, chopped\n½ tbsp. wasabi paste \nSalt and pepper to taste\n1 pc. lemon, wedged\n\nProcedure\n\n1. In a large bowl, combine chicken breast cubes, soy sauce, mirin, sugar, ginger, and garlic. Mix it well. Cover with plastic wrap, and marinate in the chiller for at least an hour.\n2. Preheat UFC Golden Fiesta Palm Oil to 170°C. While waiting, add egg and potato starch to the marinated chicken. Mix until well combined.\n3. Let excess batter drip, then deep fry chicken pieces until golden brown, about 4 minutes per batch. \n4. Drain, then sprinkle with togarashi while still hot hot.\n5. In a small bowl, combine mayonnaise, milk, parsley, and wasabi paste. Season with salt and pepper.\n6. Serve chicken karaage alongside wasabi mayo and lemon wedges.\n\nDid you know? You can now stay at home and order your groceries online at http://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
