    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Fried Chicken Day",
    "caption": "Compared to regular olive oil, pomace olive oil is made from the remaining oil in the olive pulp after the first batch of oils have been extracted — making it still flavorful and great for deep-frying.\n\nThis recipe for spicy and tangy Nashville Hot Chicken Tenders uses Doña Elena Pomace Olive Oil for a clean and delicious fry. #TheMarketplace is home to a wide selection of cooking oils and salad oils to choose from, so head over now and shop for what you need!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour and 30 minutes\nYield: 3-4 servings\nOptional: Serve with pickles\n\nIngredients\n\n400g chicken breast fillet, sliced into strips\n1 cup buttermilk\n2 tbsps. hot sauce\nSalt and pepper to taste\nOil for frying\n2 eggs, beaten\n1 ½ cup flour\n2 tbsps. garlic powder\n1 tbsp. paprika\n1 tbsp. cayenne pepper\n1 tbsp. chili powder\n2 tbsps. brown sugar\n⅔ cup Doña Elena Pomace Olive Oil\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Marinate chicken strips in buttermilk and hot sauce. Season with salt and pepper, then cover with plastic wrap, and let marinate in the chiller for at least an hour.\n2. Preheat oil to 170°C. Add eggs to marinated chicken, and mix well. \n3. Season flour with salt. Let excess batter drip, then dredge chicken strips in flour. Deep-fry until golden brown, about 4 minutes per batch. Drain and set aside. \n4. In a large bowl, combine garlic powder, paprika, cayenne pepper, chili powder, and brown sugar.\n5. In a separate pan, preheat Doña Elena Pomace Olive Oil. Add to the bowl of mixed spices, and mix to combine.\n6. Toss fried chicken tenders in the glaze. \n\nNo need to fall in line! Order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
