    "category": "RECIPE",
    "categorySource": "inferred",
    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Fried Chicken Day",
    "caption": "There’s Japanese karaage and Korean fried chicken, but have you ever tried making Vietnamese Fried Chicken Wings?\n\nWhat gives these fried chicken wings their character is the punchy, tangy, and umami-rich combination of fish sauce and tamarind. Fry them to a crisp with Marca Leon Vegetable Oil, and we guarantee you that these wings will be a frequent dish on your dining table. Head over to #TheMarketplace and get all the ingredients you need for this dish and more!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour and 30 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n300g chicken wings\n2 tbsps. fish sauce\n2 cloves garlic, grated \n4 cups Marca Leon Vegetable Oil\n½ cup cornstarch\n½ cup flour\nSalt and pepper to taste\n3 tbsps. sugar\n1 tbsp. tamarind concentrate\n½ cup water\n1 tbsp. fish sauce\n¼ cup peanuts, chopped\n2 tbsps. red chili, chopped\n½ cup cilantro leaves\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Marinate chicken wings in fish sauce and garlic for at least 1 hour in the chiller. \n2. Preheat Marca Leon Vegetable Oil to 170°C\n3. Combine cornstarch and flour, then season with salt and pepper. Dredge chicken wings with this.\n4. Deep fry chicken wings until golden brown. Drain, then set aside.\n5. In a wok, combine sugar, tamarind concentrate, water and fish sauce. Set to medium heat, then cook until thickened, about 5 minutes.\n6. Toss fried chicken wings in the glaze. Transfer to a serving plate, then top with peanuts and red chili. Garnish with cilantro. \n\nDid you know? You can now stay at home and order your groceries online at http://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
