    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Fried Chicken Day",
    "caption": "Have you tried Ayam Goreng before?\n\nThis Indonesian-style fried chicken is a very aromatic-forward dish, cooked with the use of ginger, galangal, and lemongrass. We used chicken legs for this recipe, deep-fried with heart-friendly Simply Canola Oil to provide a shattering crunch, while keeping the meat inside tender.\n\nFind Simply Canola Oil at #TheMarketplace, along with other cooking and salad oils!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour\nYield: 3-4 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 cup lemongrass, ends finely-chopped\n4 cloves garlic, crushed\n2 bay leaves\n2 tbsps. ginger, grated\n2 tbsps. galangal, grated\n2 tbsps. fish sauce\n2 cups water\n500g chicken leg quarters\n4 cups Simply Canola Oil\n1 ½ cup flour\n1 tsp. chicken powder\n¾ cup desiccated coconut\n\nProcedure\n\n1. In a pot, combine lemongrass, garlic, bay leaf, ginger, galangal, fish sauce and water. Set over medium heat. Once simmering, add in chicken leg quarters. Simmer for 20 minutes.\n2. Remove leg quarters from boiling liquid, and let cool. Preheat Simply Canola Oil to 170°C.\n3. Combine flour and chicken powder. Dredge chicken leg quarters in the flour mixture. Deep fry until golden brown, about 6 minutes. Drain, then set aside.\n4. Preheat a pan over medium high heat. Add desiccated coconut, and stir continuously until evenly browned.\n5. Top fried chicken pieces with toasted coconut. \n\nDid you know? You can now stay at home and order your groceries online at http://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
