    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "International Fried Chicken Day",
    "caption": "It’s hard to resist a classic, banging Fried Chicken Slider with Aioli.\n\nWhen the craving for a fried chicken sandwich hits, make this at home instead so you can have it fresh! For this recipe, we’re frying the chickens with La Española Olive Oil to add a little depth in terms of flavor. Olive oil comes with a number of health benefits, and we love that.\n\nGrab all the ingredients you need for this recipe, including La Española Olive Oil, the next time you shop at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour and 15 minutes\nYield: 4-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n2 egg yolks\n2 cloves garlic, grated\n¾ cup La Española Olive Oil\n1 tbsp. lemon juice\nSalt and pepper to taste\nCooking oil for deep-frying\n400g chicken thigh fillet, sliced into chunks\n½ cup flour\n½ cup cornstarch\n1 tbsp. garlic powder\n1 tsp. onion powder\n½ tsp. paprika\n2 eggs, beaten\n1 pack dinner rolls\n1 cup curly lettuce, teared \n¼ pickle chips \n\nProcedure\n\n1. In mixing bowl, whisk together egg yolks and garlic. Slowly drizzle in La Española Olive Oil while whisking continuously to emulsify. Mix in lemon juice. Season with salt and pepper, then set aside.\n2. Preheat oil to 170°C. Season chicken thigh fillet with salt and pepper. Set aside.\n3. In a bowl, combine flour, cornstarch, garlic powder, onion powder and paprika. \n4. Dredge chicken pieces in the flour mixture, then coat with with beaten eggs. Let excess liquid drip, then dredge again with the flour mixture. \n5. Deep fry chicken until golden brown, about 4 minutes per batch. Drain, then set aside. \n6. To assemble, slice dinner rolls. Fill each with lettuce, aioli, fried chicken and pickles. \n\nNo need to fall in line! Order your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
